  # ============================================================================
  # Cloudflare Workers AI ("cloudflare/", through its OpenAI-compatible endpoint)
  #
  # Checked 2026-11-22. "developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/" gives every account 10,000
  # neurons a day at no charge, reset at 00:00 UTC, counted across every model of the account together, and
  # ".../platform/limits/" 300 requests per minute for text generation. The note of the pricing page names the
  # models that need a paid billing method (the Kimi K2.6 and K2.7, GLM-5.x, DeepSeek V4.x and Inkling
  # ones): none is below. Every model below is absent from that note, so it is DEDUCED free, which the page
  # does not say, and has to be confirmed on the account before it is relied on. The allowance is small: a
  # day's neurons buy a few hundred thousand tokens of the larger models (the README says how many), which
  # is why a model that another provider serves too sits behind that provider's slot.
  #
  # The identifier of the account is not written here, nor is an "api_base": LiteLLM builds the endpoint's
  # address from "CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID", which the container is given. That makes ONE account, as Cloudflare's
  # terms require: "www.cloudflare.com/terms/" (read 2026-11-22) refuses a use "intended to circumvent
  # Service-specific usage limits, quotas", which a second account opened for more neurons would be.
  #
  # "developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/data-usage/" says Cloudflare does not train on the
  # content processed and does not retain it for a standard inference, and each model page below lists
  # zero data retention.
  #
  # Every text model below states the length of its answer: a request that names none is cut at the default
  # its model page gives, 256 tokens on most of them (read 2026-11-23, and measured through the gateway on
  # 2026-11-24 for both gpt-oss and Llama 3.3), which empties the answer of a model that reasons first. The
  # pages of GLM 4.7 Flash, Gemma 4 26B and Qwen3.8 give no default and name "max_completion_tokens" in place
  # of a deprecated "max_tokens", so their entries use it; GLM and Gemma answered uncut without one that day,
  # and carry it all the same so that one rule holds every entry. 32,768 where the context reaches 128,000
  # tokens, 8,192 under it, so that the request keeps most of the context; a client that sends its own limit
  # replaces it. "check_compose_template.py" refuses a text entry of Cloudflare without one.
  #
  # Looked at the same day and not routed: Kimi, GLM-5 and DeepSeek V4, which are paid per the note above;
  # Nemotron 3 120B, whose page says "Deprecated 11/20/2026" while LiteLLM's model map still lists it. Qwen 3.8 27B
  # is routed below although LiteLLM's model map does not list it and it cannot be steered: asked a hard question on
  # 2026-11-22 with "reasoning_effort" low and xhigh, and with "chat_template_kwargs" turning thinking off, it answered
  # in 2,547, 1,770 and 2,616 tokens over 109, 81 and 85 seconds, every time with a reasoning field, so no setting
  # shortens it, which is why it stands behind its twins.
