  # UNVERIFIED: the page says it of the service, not model by model. LiteLLM's "nvidia_nim/" provider calls
  # NVIDIA's own endpoint by default (read in its source), so no entry writes an "api_base". Each entry's tool
  # support and context length are those its model card on the catalogue declares in its capability data (read
  # that day). That LiteLLM forwards tools to this provider was shown against a stand-in server; that the
