{% if has.Cent_AI %}
  # ============================================================================
  # Cent AI ("openai/" through its OpenAI-compatible endpoint, one free model)
  #
  # Checked 2026-11-22. Cent AI is a reseller of models. LiteLLM has no provider of that name, so the entry is
  # "openai/<id>" with an "api_base": LiteLLM cuts the prefix once and the id reaches Cent AI as written, the
  # ":free" included. A real call to it answered that day, from the maintainer's own test; tool calls through it
  # were not tried.
  #
  # Its home page says "Free until Nov 30 · no daily limit" and says nothing of what follows. The catalogue lists
  # the model at 0 $, and whether it is billed at its rate after that is UNVERIFIED. It is routed until then and
  # looked at again on 2026-12-01. A key given a spending limit on Cent AI's key page keeps a billed call from
  # costing anything: the call then fails and the cascade moves on, so such a limit is what to set on the key
  # given here. The site also draws one free "event" model a day, whose id changes every day: it cannot be
  # routed, and nothing here names it.
  #
  # The entry sets no level: no page of Cent AI read on 2026-11-24 says which "reasoning_effort" values the model
  # takes.
  #
  # The operator is an individual whose terms are a draft, and the requests are relayed to vendors it does not
  # name: whoever gives the key lets a third party read the prompts. One account only.
  # ============================================================================
  # Tencent's Hy4 Flash, as far as its name says. No Artificial Analysis record carries that name (its one
  # Tencent record, "Tencent Hy4", is the model Tencent lists beside this one, not this one), and neither the
  # capabilities index nor a code benchmark of Epoch AI holds it (both read 2026-11-21), so no figure places it:
  # it closes the free members of "Auto-Pro", "Auto-Flash" and "Auto-Flash-Lite", behind those that have a figure or a twin
  # and ahead of OVHcloud's, and is in no other router, its tool calls being untried. It REASONS before it answers, so no "max_tokens" is set on it
  # and a caller must not cap it low: with 20 the answer was cut, with a finish reason of "length".
  - model_name: hy4-flash-cent-ai
    model_info:
      access_groups: ["LLM", "Public-Data-Only"]
      max_input_tokens: 1048576
    litellm_params:
      model: openai/hy4-flash:free
      api_base: "https://api.cent-ai.dev/v1"
      litellm_credential_name: "cent-ai"

{% endif %}

{% if has.Aion_Labs %}
  # ============================================================================
  # Aion Labs ("openai/" through its OpenAI-compatible endpoint, models for role-play and fiction)
  #
  # Checked 2026-11-23. Aion Labs' public catalogue, "api.aionlabs.ai/v1/models" (no key), lists these six text
  # models, all "text->text", all priced per token, none moderated ("is_moderated": false), and its documentation
  # gives the same base address, "https://api.aionlabs.ai/v1". LiteLLM has no provider of that name, so each entry is
  # "openai/<id>" with an "api_base": LiteLLM cuts the prefix once and the id, "aion-labs/<model>", reaches Aion Labs
  # as written. No call was made while writing this, there being no key: the form is the one of the provider's own
  # quickstart.
  #
  # Aion Labs describes these models as tuned for immersive role-play and storytelling, handling "mature and darker
  # themes", and moderates nothing. That is why they are kept apart: their access group is "Fiction", not "LLM", so
  # that no key holding "LLM" reaches them, and "Auto-Fiction" is the only router that holds them, in no other
  # cascade. A key reaches them when "Fiction" or "Auto-Fiction" is named in its models.
  #
  # The free tier is the allowance of the whole account, not a price of a model: 15 requests and 20,000 tokens a
  # minute, and 20,000 tokens a day, all six models together ("aionlabs.ai/docs/rate-limits/"), which a few
  # requests to a model that reasons use up. The key is activated by verifying a payment card that is never
  # charged, one card for one free account, and the terms ("aionlabs.ai/terms/", of 2026-10-17) call free use
  # "a courtesy that we may change or withdraw at any time". They allow one account, forbid sharing the key itself
  # and allow a gateway of one's own; the privacy policy says the content of a request is neither stored nor used
  # to train models. The models are listed at a price, and any credit top-up moves the account to a tier with no daily
  # token limit, where calls are billed at those prices: give the account none.
  #
  # Tokens are counted, and thinking spends them, so no entry sets a level: each model keeps the balance its
  # maker chose, the provider's default.
  # ============================================================================
  # The newest and largest first, which is the order of "Auto-Fiction". A multi-model system of the GLM family,
  # 262,144 tokens of context. No figure is read for any of these models, so none places them: the contracts of the
  # routers say why.
  - model_name: aion-3-5-aion-labs
    model_info:
