{% if has.Vercel_AI_Gateway %}
  # ============================================================================
  # Vercel AI Gateway ("vercel_ai_gateway/", LiteLLM's own provider of that name, a free monthly credit)
  #
  # Checked 2026-11-24. LiteLLM's provider calls Vercel's OpenAI-compatible base, "https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1",
  # on its own (read in its source), so no entry writes an "api_base", and it reads "VERCEL_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY" when
  # an entry names no key; each entry names it all the same, since the check of account isolation reads the variable
  # of an entry. The model is the id the gateway lists, "<creator>/<model>". Measured with the account's key that
  # day: "openai/gpt-5-mini", "openai/gpt-5", "google/gemini-2.5-flash" and "mistral/mistral-large-3" answered, and
  # "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5", which is outside the free tier, answered 403. Tool calls through these entries
  # are untried, and no call was made from the session that wrote this, which holds no key.
  #
  # The free tier ("vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/pricing" and its FAQ, read that day) is "a monthly included credit, not
  # an expiring trial", on a subset of the models: any other answers 403 "Free tier users do not have access to this
  # model". The amount is on no page read (the account showed a balance of 5 USD before its first request), and the
  # free tier's rate limits per model, "lower" than the paid tier's, are given no figure. The credit needs a payment
  # method on the team (403 "customer_verification_required" without one). The account is prepaid: the card is charged
  # only for a purchase of credit or by Auto-reload, which is off by default, and a request with no credit answers 402.
  # The first purchase of credit moves the team to the paid tier and ends the free monthly credit for good, so none is
  # to be made and Auto-reload is to stay off.
  #
  # The credit is ONE pool for every entry below, and small: once it is spent each of them answers 402, and the
  # cascade moves on to the next member, a refusal that costs a fraction of a second apiece. The entries are therefore
  # placed by their figures among the other free members, and none is put ahead of them for being a second pool.
  # Each is a chat model on the models page filtered to the free tier ("vercel.com/ai-gateway/models?freeTier=true",
  # read that day) that a figure places: an Artificial Analysis index, or Epoch AI's capabilities index where that has
  # none, which the contracts of the routers give with their day. They are in "Auto-Pro", "Auto-Flash" and
  # "Auto-Flash-Lite", and in neither "Auto-Code" nor "Auto-Claude-Code": tool calls through the gateway are untried,
  # and an agent would spend the credit in no time. Every chat model of the free tier that the catalogue lists is
  # here: placed by its figure where one applies, and at the tail of the free members of "Auto-Flash" and of
  # "Auto-Flash-Lite", behind the members that have one, where none does or the level of the one there is was never
  # verified (the records of Muse Ember and Mistral Small, say, which are at levels the catalogue does not say it
